diff --git a/docs/specs/source-loading.md b/docs/specs/source-loading.md
index 1e1a8b3..89156e6 100644
--- a/docs/specs/source-loading.md
+++ b/docs/specs/source-loading.md
@@ -53,3 +53,8 @@ buildLifeboat creates include-once loaders with private chunk locals and shared
 Real section/endsection comments support EXACT (default), PATTERN using bounded Lua pattern matching, instance thresholds and named/nested regions. Strings and ordinary comments do not count as code references. __LB_SIMULATOR_ONLY__ and explicit Storm Code managed setup blocks are removed before resolving game dependencies, independently of minification. Offsets/newlines are preserved during removal and non-minified code uses the existing link source map; no optimization source map is provided. Pattern/depth/module/size budgets fail visibly rather than silently keep or delete ambiguous sections.
 
 Source inspection is limited to 2 MiB, 200,000 lexical tokens and bounded syntax/literal nesting. It exposes exact i64 strings, binary64 bits and byte strings. It is opt-in and does not change default optimization parsing or search settings.
+
+
+## Tagged metadata in project builds (additive, not yet released)
+
+ProjectCompileOptions.metadataTag removes only a leading long comment whose first content line exactly matches the given tag. The shared lexer supplies the comment ranges; embedded strings and unrelated comments are not removed. The operation preserves UTF-8 byte positions and newlines for the linker, and Source Map sourcesContent remains the original input. Both ordinary return-valued builds and LifeBoat include-once builds use the same metadata routine as Addon builds. The default without metadataTag retains the earlier behavior and does not clone the project for preprocessing. Development-only LifeBoat sections are still removed only by the LifeBoat/Addon linker, not by the normal static module linker.
